  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n**Model tier:** low\n\n## Context\n\nModel tier rationale: This changes three existing fixture DDL statements to the established IF EXISTS pattern.\n\n- PR #1134, finding `f20e822718`, `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/mailIdentityPerTenant.test.ts:45`: The helper and two test bodies unconditionally drop a legacy index that #1065 is scheduled to remove.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd `IF EXISTS` to all three `DROP INDEX mail_message_meta_provider_msg_uq` statements: the conditional drop in `twoTenantsAsRuntimeRole` and the setup of the same-tenant provider-conflict and other-unique-index tests. Preserve their current rollback isolation, the dropLegacyIndex option and conflict assertions. Verify the affected setup with the legacy index present and with it pre-removed inside a rolled-back fixture.\n\n## Touches\n\n- backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/mailIdentityPerTenant.test.ts (three legacy-index drops and their setup verification only)\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\nMaking the reported optional-index removal repeatable in this test suite.\n\n### Out of scope\n\nThe migration delivered by #1065, new index definitions, changes to conflict classification and other legacy-index fixtures.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- For finding `f20e822718`, all three affected setup paths succeed whether mail_message_meta_provider_msg_uq exists or is already absent; the existing conflict and two-tenant identity cases still pass.\n\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=1134 key=f20e822718 -->",
